|en
|year=2019
|author=Lou Marinoff
|title=On Human Conflict: The Philosophical Foundations of War and Peace
|publisher=Rowman & Littlefield
|isbn=9780761871064
|page=452
|passage={{...}} he chose instead to suffer even greater personal pain, with unimaginable fortitude and resolve, albeit for a shorter time. Thus he '''died''' a small death, in order to benefit the living. Similarly, a small and voluntary death was '''died''' by Socrates.}}
# {{lb|en|video games|slang}} To [[lose]] or be eliminated from a game, particularly with a deathlike animation.
#* {{quote-web|en|year=1995|url=https://www.csoon.com/issue3/slob.htm|title=Slobzone|site=Coming Soon! magazine|genre=video game review|passage=Of course, Nazis are not present in this game. Instead, we have animals that will try to cover you with dirt. As soon as you get too dirty, you will '''die'''.}}
#*{{quote-av|en|year=2009|author=Brian Sulpher|platform=youtube|time=9:15–9:30|title=Onto Doom And Gloom|url=https://youtube.com/f0_QvXjhpto|passage=Oh look, I just '''died'''.{{...}}I missed that jump again! That was dumb! Hey, I just '''died''' on the same freakin' Zinger.|genre=video game playthrough}}
#: {{ux|en|Whenever my brother '''dies''', he [[ragequit|ragequits]].}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive|figuratively}} To [[yearn]] intensely.
#: {{ux|en|I'm '''dying''' for a packet of crisps.}}
#: {{ux|en|I'm '''dying''' for a piss.}}
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Much Ado About Nothing|III|II|passage=Yes, and his ill conditions; and in despite of all, '''dies''' for him.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2004|author=Paul Joseph Draus|title=Consumed in the city: observing tuberculosis at century's end|page=168
|passage=I could see that he was dying, '''dying''' for a cigarette, '''dying''' for a fix maybe, '''dying''' for a little bit of freedom, but trapped in a hospital bed and a sick body.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive|uncommon|idiomatic}} To be or become hated or utterly ignored or [[cut off]], as if [[dead]].
#: {{ux|en|The day our sister eloped, she '''died''' to our mother.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2015|author=Emily Duvall|title=Inclusions|page=150
|passage="My dad {{...}} beat us until we couldn't sit down." {{...}} "What about your mother?" {{...}} "She's alive. {{...}} My aunt visits her once a year, but I don't ask about my mother. She '''died''' to me the day she chose my father over protecting us." Luke's voice hitched with emotion.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2017|author=Mike Hoornstra|title=Descent into the Maelstrom|page=366
|passage="You haven't been my son since you were ten years old. That boy '''died''' to me the day he ran away. I don't know you. You are merely a shell that resembles someone I used to know, but you are dead to me. You are the bringer of pain and death. Leave me be. Leave me with my son, Jyosh." "Mother..." Barlun pleaded.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive|figuratively}} To become [[spiritually]] [[dead]]; to [[lose]] [[hope]].
#: {{ux|en|He '''died''' a little inside each time she refused to speak to him.}}
#* {{quote-song|en|title=Ghost|author=w:Ingrid Michaelson|album=w:Human Again|year=2011|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VAsnpp_MDog|text=Do you know that I went down / To the ground / Landed on both my broken-hearted knees... / {{...}}I didn't even cry / 'Cause pieces of me had already '''died'''}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive|colloquial|hyperbolic}} To be [[mortified]] or [[shocked]] by a situation.
#: {{ux|en|If anyone sees me wearing this ridiculous outfit, I'll '''die'''.}}
# {{senseid|en|hyperbolic}}{{lb|en|intransitive|figurative|hyperbolic}} To be so [[overcome]] with [[emotion]] or [[laughter]] as to be [[incapacitated]].
#: {{ux|en|When I found out my two favorite musicians would be recording an album together, I literally planned my own funeral arrangements and '''died'''.}}
#* '''1976''', an anchorman on Channel Five in California, quoted in ''[https://books.google.com/books?id=g19wAAAAIAAJ Journal and Newsletter] [of the] California Classical Association, Northern Section'':
#*: I literally '''died''' when I saw that.
# {{lb|en|intransitive|of a|machine}} To [[stop]] [[work]]ing; to [[break down]] or otherwise lose "vitality".
#: {{ux|en|My car '''died''' in the middle of the freeway this morning.}}
#: {{ux|en|Sorry I couldn't call you. My phone '''died'''.}}
#: {{ux|en|My battery '''died''' and my charger was at home.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive|of a|computer program}} To [[abort]], to [[terminate]] (as an [[error]] [[condition]]).
# {{lb|en|intransitive|of a|legislative bill or resolution}} To [[expire]] at the [[end]] of the [[session]] of a [[legislature]] without having been brought to a [[vote]].
#: {{ux|en|The proposed gas tax '''died''' after the powerful rural senator refused to let it out of committee.}}
# To [[perish]]; to [[cease]] to [[exist]]; to become [[lost]] or [[extinct]].
#* {{RQ:Spectator|VI|594|September 15 1714|passage=letting the secret '''die''' within his own breast}}
#* {{RQ:Tennyson Princess
|passage=Great deeds cannot '''die'''.}}
#* {{RQ:Dunsany Pegana||88|Through all the Worlds are sounds, the noises of moving, and the echoes of voices and song; but upon the River is no sound ever heard, for there all echoes '''die'''.}}
# To [[sink]]; to [[faint]]; to [[pine]]; to [[languish]], with [[weakness]], [[discouragement]], [[love]], etc.
#* {{RQ:KJV|1 Samuel|25|37|passage=But it came to passe in the morning, when the wine was gone out of Nabal, and his wife had told him these things, that his heart '''died''' within him, and he became as a stone.}}
#* {{quote-song|en|author=w:Darby Slick|authorlabel=no|title={{w|Somebody to Love (Jefferson Airplane song)|Somebody to Love}}|album=w:Surrealistic Pillow|year=1965|year_published=1967|artist=w:Jefferson Airplane|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=a-C9pUGszsw|text=When the truth is found to be lies / And all the joy within you '''dies''' / Don't you want somebody to love? / Don't you need somebody to love?}}
# {{lb|en|often with "to"}} To become [[indifferent]]; to [[cease]] to be [[subject]].
#: {{ux|en|to '''die''' to pleasure or to sin}}
# {{lb|en|architecture}} To [[disappear]] [[gradually]] in another [[surface]], as where [[moulding]]s are [[lost]] in a [[sloped]] or [[curved]] [[face]].
# To become [[vapid]], [[flat]], or [[spiritless]], as [[liquor]].
# {{lb|en|of a stand-up comedian or a joke|slang}} To [[fail]] to [[evoke]] [[laughter]] from the [[audience]].
#: {{ux|en|Then there was that time I '''died''' onstage in Montreal...}}

